\title{Cartesian product}
\date{2026-02-23T11:55:00Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{If #{A} and #{B} are sets, the \em{(Cartesian) product} of #{A} and #{B}, written #{A \times B}, is the set of all possible ordered pairs of elements from #{A} and #{B}. That is, ##{A \times B = \{ (a, b) \mid a \in A, b \in B \}.}}
